From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: host: xhci: fix A733 HCRST timeout with a bounded reset retry

On the Allwinner A733, USBCMD.HCRST only completes when
SERDES_SUBSYS_APP + 0x0008 holds 0x00030010 (bit 21,
USB3P1_USB2P0_UTMI_CLK_SEL, clear), selecting the U2P0 femtoPHY as the
USB2 UTMI clock source.

The first xHCI probe can run before sunxi-cadence-combophy has enabled
the SerDes 1.8 V supply and clocks.  Until then the SerDes is gated and
writes to its register file are silently dropped, so HCRST times out
with -ETIMEDOUT ("can't setup: -110").  Two approaches were measured on
a Radxa Cubie A7A:

  * Deferring the probe (-EPROBE_DEFER) until U2P0_PHYSTS bit 3 is set
    removes the -110 but leaves xhci-hcd.0.auto permanently in
    devices_deferred: the driver core does not retry this platform
    device reliably on this board.  A manual bind afterwards succeeds
    immediately, which proves the hardware is ready by then.
  * Re-asserting the word only in xhci_reset() is not sufficient either,
    because that write also happens before the SerDes is powered.

Fix it without depending on probe retries:

  * xhci_plat_probe() re-asserts the word early but never defers.
  * xhci_reset() re-asserts the word immediately before CMD_RESET, keeps
    the first handshake short (1 s) on A733, and on failure re-asserts
    the word again and retries with the full timeout.  By then
    sunxi-cadence-combophy has powered the SerDes, so the write sticks
    and the controller comes out of reset.

Measured on the board: no -110, no permanently deferred probe, both
root hubs register and the on-board Terminus hub (1a40:0101)
enumerates.  The word is idempotent, so later xhci_reset() calls
(resume, error recovery) are unaffected.

NOTE: this is out-of-tree board-enablement glue. Before any upstream
submission the hard-coded SoC register accesses must be replaced by
DT-described clock/reset/power-domain/PHY providers and the probe
ordering must be expressed as a DT dependency (fw_devlink).

Signed-off-by: Juanesf <juanesf91@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci.c | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
@@ -199,6 +199,25 @@
 	}
 
 	xhci_dbg_trace(xhci, trace_xhci_dbg_init, "// Reset the HC");
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI
+	/*
+	 * Allwinner A733: the USB2 port is clocked from the U2P0 femtoPHY,
+	 * which requires SERDES_SUBSYS_APP + 0x0008 bit 21
+	 * (USB3P1_USB2P0_UTMI_CLK_SEL) to be clear.  Re-assert the golden
+	 * word 0x00030010 immediately before CMD_RESET so it wins over any
+	 * later SerDes programming.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun60i-a733")) {
+		void __iomem *serdes = ioremap(0x06c00000, 0x1000);
+
+		if (serdes) {
+			writel(0x00030010, serdes + 0x0008);
+			iounmap(serdes);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 	command = readl(&xhci->op_regs->command);
 	command |= CMD_RESET;
 	writel(command, &xhci->op_regs->command);
@@ -213,7 +232,44 @@
 	if (xhci->quirks & XHCI_INTEL_HOST)
 		udelay(1000);
 
-	ret = xhci_handshake(&xhci->op_regs->command, CMD_RESET, 0, timeout_us);
+	{
+		u64 first_timeout = timeout_us;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI
+		/*
+		 * On A733 the first probe can run before
+		 * sunxi-cadence-combophy has enabled the SerDes supplies
+		 * and clocks; writes to a gated SerDes are dropped, so
+		 * HCRST times out.  Keep the first handshake short, then
+		 * re-assert the word (now that the SerDes is powered) and
+		 * retry with the full timeout.  A -EPROBE_DEFER was tried
+		 * instead and measured to leave the controller
+		 * permanently in devices_deferred.
+		 */
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun60i-a733"))
+			first_timeout = min_t(u64, timeout_us, 1000000);
+#endif
+
+		ret = xhci_handshake(&xhci->op_regs->command, CMD_RESET, 0,
+				     first_timeout);
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI
+		if (ret &&
+		    of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun60i-a733")) {
+			void __iomem *serdes = ioremap(0x06c00000, 0x1000);
+
+			if (serdes) {
+				writel(0x00030010, serdes + 0x0008);
+				iounmap(serdes);
+			}
+			writel(command, &xhci->op_regs->command);
+			if (xhci->quirks & XHCI_INTEL_HOST)
+				udelay(1000);
+			ret = xhci_handshake(&xhci->op_regs->command,
+					     CMD_RESET, 0, timeout_us);
+		}
+#endif
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/pci.h>
@@ -168,6 +169,25 @@
 	if (usb_disabled())
 		return -ENODEV;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI
+	/*
+	 * Allwinner A733: re-assert SERDES_SUBSYS_APP + 0x0008 early.  Do
+	 * not defer this probe based on a PHY status bit: measured on the
+	 * board, a -EPROBE_DEFER here leaves xhci-hcd.0.auto permanently in
+	 * devices_deferred (the driver core does not retry it reliably),
+	 * while the SerDes is in fact ready a moment later.  xhci_reset()
+	 * re-asserts the word again and retries HCRST if needed.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("allwinner,sun60i-a733")) {
+		void __iomem *serdes = ioremap(0x06c00000, 0x1000);
+
+		if (serdes) {
+			writel(0x00030010, serdes + 0x0008);
+			iounmap(serdes);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 	driver = &xhci_plat_hc_driver;
 
 	irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
